WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.957
The window function concepts from Module 11 transfer to Spark SQL.

00:00:04.957 --> 00:00:07.672
PARTITION BY defines groups. ORDER BY defines sequence.

00:00:07.672 --> 00:00:11.712
LAG and LEAD provide previous and next values.

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:14.552
Frames define running or moving calculations.

00:00:14.552 --> 00:00:22.522
In Spark, these are powerful, but they may also require sorting and data movement.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:27.012
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:32.642
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:32.642 --> 00:00:34.587
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:43.467
In a real setting such as a healthcare analytics platform processing large longitudinal event tables,

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:49.562
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:49.562 --> 00:00:51.742
before discussing syntax.

00:00:51.742 --> 00:00:58.130
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
